{"id":"a4ffdd49-a024-4414-bfe6-c245b9adb872","object":"chat.completion","created":1784999531,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    # Validate input structure\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must be a dictionary\\\")\\n    if 'nodes' not in case or 'core_distance' not in case or 'distances' not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case missing required fields: nodes, core_distance, distances\\\")\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core = case['core_distance']\\n    raw_edges = case['distances']\\n    # Validate nodes and core_distance\\n    if not isinstance(nodes, list) or len(nodes) == 0:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"nodes must be a non-empty list\\\")\\n    if set(nodes) != set(core.keys()):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"core_distance keys must exactly match nodes\\\")\\n    # Build mutual reachability edges\\n    edge_list = []\\n    for u, v, d in raw_edges:\\n        if u not in core or v not in core:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Edge endpoint {u} or {v} not in nodes\\\")\\n        # Canonical order for tie-breaking\\n        if u < v:\\n            a, b = u, v\\n        else:\\n            a, b = v, u\\n        w = max(core[a], core[b], d)\\n        edge_list.append((w, a, b))\\n    # Sort by weight, then by min node, then by max node (lexicographic)\\n    edge_list.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1], x[2]))\\n    # Union-Find\\n    parent = {n: n for n in nodes}\\n    rank = {n: 0 for n in nodes}\\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]  # path compression\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\\n            parent[rx] = ry\\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n        else:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n    for w, a, b in edge_list:\\n        if union(a, b):\\n            mst_edges.append([a, b, w])\\n            total_weight += w\\n            if len(mst_edges) == len(nodes) - 1:\\n                break\\n    # Check connectivity\\n    if len(mst_edges) != len(nodes) - 1:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Graph is disconnected: cannot build MST\\\")\\n    return {\\n        \\\"mst_edges\\\": mst_edges,\\n        \\\"total_weight\\\": total_weight\\n    }\\n\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) according to the specification. Input case has fields: nodes (list of strings), core_distance (dict mapping node to float), distances (list of [str, str, float] edges). Compute mutual reachability as max(core_left, core_right, distance). Build an undirected graph, sort edges by (mutual_reachability, min_node, max_node). Then Kruskal MST. Return mst_edges (list of [node1, node2, weight]) and total_weight (sum of weights). Ensure weight is number. Node identifiers are strings. Use deterministic tie-breaking: sort by weight, then lexicographically by smaller node, then larger node. Use union-find with path compression and union by size. Reject if graph disconnected (must have exactly n-1 edges after algorithm). Raise ValueError if disconnected or missing fields. Output exactly JSON matching schema. Implement in Python using standard library only. No external libs. Encode as JSON string.\n\nI'll write a clean implementation. Ensure not to mutate case. Use list of edges computed from distances and core_distance. Compute mutual_reachability for each undirected pair (sorted pair). Build list of (weight, u, v) tuples, then sort. Run Kruskal: initialize parent dict for each node. Function find(x). For each edge in sorted order, if find(u) != find(v), union, add to mst_edges, accumulate total_weight. After processing, check if len(mst_edges) == len(nodes) - 1. Else raise ValueError('Graph is disconnected').\n\nReturn {'mst_edges': mst_edges, 'total_weight': total_weight}.\n\nEdge case: duplicate edges? The input distances list may not have both directions, assume undirected. We'll use sorted endpoints.\n\nAlso ensure core_distance dict covers all nodes.\n\nImplementation details: use case['nodes'] etc.\n\nWrite code as string with proper escaping for JSON. The output must be a JSON object with key \"implementation\". So we produce {\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    ...\"} etc.\n\nLet's write the Python code.\n\nWe'll include error handling: check that case has 'nodes', 'core_distance', 'distances'. Check nodes list and core_distance keys match. Otherwise raise ValueError.\n\nUse sorted for tie-breaking.\n\nWrite union-find class or just functions.\n\nMake sure to not use recursion depth issue, use iterative find.\n\nWrite final answer.\n\nI'll produce the JSON."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2017,"completion_tokens":1200,"total_tokens":3217,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1920},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":516},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1920,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":97},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}